id: pm-rrwh2o
title: "Combining an annotation or linked-artifact mutation with a universal output control is refused untyped: code command_failed and pm --help examples instead of a stable code and a retry without the control"
description: "Found 2026-11-08 while verifying PR 1685 review findings. validateReadOutputOptions (src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts) refuses a comments, notes, learnings, files, docs or package-catalog mutation combined with a universal output control (--output-budget, --output-cursor, --output-limit, --output-include, --output-session) with the message \"Universal output controls cannot be combined with a <command> mutation.\" The refusal carries no typed code. pm learnings <id> --add x --output-cursor bad --json reports code command_failed, required \"Adjust command input or tracker state and retry.\" and examples \"pm --help\" and \"pm <command> --help\". So an agent cannot key its recovery on the refusal, and the guidance never says what to do: run the mutation without the output control, or read with the output control after the write. Measured on the PR 1685 head with the built CLI in a sandbox tracker. Expected: a stable code (for example read_output_mutation_conflict), the offending output flags, and a suggested retry without them, through CLI, SDK and MCP. The refusal-closure census should count the new code. Duplicate check: searched universal output controls mutation refusal code. pm-479ggz (closed) rejected the controls for package manage diagnostics, and pm-f05lsg (open) measures recovery closure in general. Neither types this refusal."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,read-output,recovery,refusals
